xv6 is a re-implementation of Dennis Ritchie's and Ken Thompson's Unix
Version 6 (v6).  xv6 loosely follows the structure and style of v6,
but is implemented for real multiprocessing on Raspberry Pi 3
hardware (ARMv8-A/Cortex-A53, running in AArch32 compatibility mode -
a 32-bit kernel, not a 64-bit one), using ANSI C.  Boots both under
QEMU and on real Raspberry Pi 3 hardware, with an interactive shell
and a working USB stack (vendored USPi).

ACKNOWLEDGMENTS

See README.common at the top of this repository for the acknowledgments
shared by every port here - John Lions's Commentary, the contributor
list, and the copyright.  What follows is specific to this port.

BUILDING AND RUNNING XV6

From the repository root: run ./configure once (it detects an ARM
cross toolchain and a qemu-system-arm on this machine), then
`make build-arm-pi3`, `make run-arm-pi3` (interactive shell under
QEMU), or `make test-arm-pi3` (boots headless and runs the usertests
suite).  See this directory's own Makefile for the real-hardware
(SD card image) target.
